{
  "name": "Reactivation Campaign",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nA customer list goes in. People you must not or should not contact are taken\nout - **with the reason showing on the canvas**. Whoever is left gets a message\nwritten from their own service history, and a person approves it.\n\n**The money is in the suppression list, not the copy.** Anyone can write \"we\nmiss you\". Not texting the wrong people is the job.\n\nTen customers in. Five contacted, five left alone.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e5000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1560,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why the SMS node is greyed out\n\n**Text messages are not email.** A marketing text needs prior express written\nconsent (TCPA - $500 to $1,500 per message), the number has to be registered\nwith the carriers (A2P 10DLC), STOP has to work, and 8am-9pm is the recipient's\nlocal time, not yours.\n\nEmail is far more permissive: CAN-SPAM lets you contact past customers, with an\nunsubscribe link and a postal address.\n\nSo the Twilio node is **disabled on purpose**. Two things before anyone enables\nit: the business can show you its consent records, and 10DLC registration is\ndone. Building the sender takes ten minutes. Knowing not to fire it is the part\nworth paying for.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "e5000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1060,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Running it\n\n`Customer List` and both writing steps have **pinned data**, so the whole thing\nruns with no accounts connected. Unpin a node to make it call out for real.\n\nDates are measured from a fixed run date of 2026-08-29 so the demo always\ntells the same story. Swap `DateTime.fromISO('2026-08-29')` for `$now` in\n*How Long Since We Saw Them* to run it against real dates.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "e5000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
